//
// Everything this template styles lives in quartz/styles/custom/, one file per
// component, loaded in the order listed in the block above. Nothing is styled
// here directly - this file only holds the import order and this note.
//
// Two things are worth knowing before changing anything:
//
//   • No colour and no measure of the design is written literally in those
//     files. Both come from CSS variables, which the app manages under
//     "Stile → Variablen" (the `css-vars` block further down this file). Change
//     --tpl-space-md there and every gap in the site follows. What does stand
//     literally is named and accounted for: the callout and syntax colours,
//     because they mean status rather than palette; hairlines; and the
//     breakpoints, since a media query cannot read a variable.
//
//   • The colours were measured, not chosen by eye: every text/background pair
